update  ProgressNote
set updatedby = 'CJAMS-57676', updatedon = now(),description = '<p>T.Gay phoned D. Warr at 17:11 and left a voicemail.  Soon after the father returned the workers call with his mother on the line.  </p><p><span style="color:#000000;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">T. Warr and D. Warr phoned T.Gay to provide the worker with a history of family dynamics.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Majority of the discussion was completed by T.Warr.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">The family began the interview by reporting that they had traveled to the Circuit Court earlier that day to inquire about custody and paternity testing.&nbsp; The family was instructed to return "early" another day with the expectation to pay $175 file a petition to have Neveah brought in for a blood test.&nbsp; D. Warr was 17 years old when Neveah was conceived.&nbsp; He told his family about the baby when Neveah was six months old.&nbsp; T. Warr reported being caregiver of Neveah for months at a time, even when the Warrs lived in Tapphannock, VA.&nbsp; The worker asked if the family had safety concerns regarding S. Helmick.&nbsp; T.Warr responded she had concerns but would not divulge them for fear of Neveah being put into foster care.&nbsp; T.Warr did tell the worker that P. Abrams is critical of Neveah and locks her in the basement when she is the childs caregiver, or give the child melatonin to make her sleep.&nbsp; Prior to Neveah becoming school-aged, S. Helmick was a stay-at-home parent.&nbsp; Once Neveah reached school age "DSS required" S. Helmick to obtain employment.&nbsp; S. Helmick began working evenings and P. Abrams works at night.<br>The worker asked T.Warr to explain the events that lead to Neveahs initial disclosure.&nbsp; According to the grandmother&nbsp; T. Warr was giving Neveah a bath, Neveah said, "I hurt" in reference to her vagina.&nbsp; T. Warr reported opening the childs legs to assess and observed that the vaginal opening appeared to be "split".&nbsp; T.Warr asked who had been "messing" with her and Neveah responded "Dakari". on Sunday 9/1/24 she told S. Helmick that Neveah disclosed being touched.&nbsp; T. Warr urged the parent to take the child to the doctor. S. Helmick responded, "I dont know where they get this nasty stuff from.&nbsp; They dont get it from me" and promised to take the child the next day.&nbsp; T.Warr spoke to S. Helmick again on 9/4, but the parent seemed resistant to getting medical attention for her daughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">D. Warr also questioned Neveah by asking if she had been touched.&nbsp; Neveah did not answer.&nbsp; When the father asked if she did it herself, the child responded, "No, BaBa did it". According to the Warrs, BaBa is how Neveah refers to her brothers.&nbsp; When asked which brother, she replied "Dakari".&nbsp; S. Helmick reportedly called Neveah a "liar" and denied that either of her sons would touch Neveah.&nbsp; S. Helmick told the family that she had questioned the boys and they began crying, which is how she knew they were being truthful.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000;"><span style="background-color:transparent;">On 10/11, the Warrs picked up Neveah for a visit.&nbsp; While preparing for bed, Neveah approached her paternal grandmother and said, "Mom-Mom, I hurt."&nbsp; T. Warr removed the childs underwear and assessed her vulva.&nbsp; T. Warr described the childs genitalia as "really red", "kinda open", and secreting a "white, cottage cheese-like discharge".&nbsp; The grandparent took Neveah to the emergency room the next morning.&nbsp; At Sinai, the visit was treated as a "rape case".&nbsp; Neveahs vagina was swabbed and a urine sample taken.&nbsp; The child was diagnosed with a UTI, bacterial infection, and yeast infection.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><br></p>' 
where progressnoteid = 'd7f3c249-7e60-4f2b-93a7-31efc55a7eed' and activeflag = 1;

